So just knowing, when you
strike out on your goal,

00:12:29.305 --> 00:12:32.051
you're going to have to
get ready for flexibility.

00:12:32.051 --> 00:12:34.344
Because there's going
to be detours, pitfalls,

00:12:34.344 --> 00:12:37.927
stop signs, men working,
or delays, detours

00:12:39.461 --> 00:12:42.834
going around, that has to be expected.

00:12:42.834 --> 00:12:44.894
Terrell, who's our floor manager here,

00:12:44.894 --> 00:12:49.119
he runs the entire set, his
first job out of high school

00:12:49.119 --> 00:12:52.243
was at Magic Johnson's Theater in L.A.

00:12:52.243 --> 00:12:54.670
That was his first job, for four years.

00:12:54.670 --> 00:12:58.874
He swept floors, cleaned up
the theater for four years.

00:12:58.874 --> 00:13:02.132
Boy runs a TV show now, ain't that great?

00:13:02.132 --> 00:13:06.299
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:13:07.976 --> 00:13:11.368
See, the hustle man, somebody sent me

00:13:11.368 --> 00:13:14.168
a wonderful sign one
day, it was like a sign

00:13:14.168 --> 00:13:18.027
that goes in front of a
house that's for sale.

00:13:18.027 --> 00:13:22.194
It says, "The dream is free,
the hustle is sold separately."

00:13:24.196 --> 00:13:26.974
And that's so true, man, you never,

00:13:26.974 --> 00:13:30.551
you can never give up, you don't ever know

00:13:30.551 --> 00:13:35.019
whren God is just waiting
on you to pass the test.

00:13:35.019 --> 00:13:37.787
But you have to stay with something

00:13:37.787 --> 00:13:40.109
and go through the test to get to the end.

00:13:40.109 --> 00:13:43.933
See, if you quit, there's
no way you'll ever know.

00:13:43.933 --> 00:13:46.013
You have to keep putting one
foot in front of the other,

00:13:46.013 --> 00:13:47.939
even if you don't know the way.

00:13:47.939 --> 00:13:50.129
It's not your job to know the way.

00:13:50.129 --> 00:13:53.160
It's your job to believe,
that's why people mess up

00:13:53.160 --> 00:13:55.432
as people, you try to figure it out.

00:13:55.432 --> 00:13:58.138
Show me the scripture that
tells you to figure it out.

00:13:58.138 --> 00:13:59.607
Where is that scripture at?

00:13:59.607 --> 00:14:01.589
There's no scripture that
tells you to figure it out.

00:14:01.589 --> 00:14:04.016
It tells you to ask and believe.

00:14:04.016 --> 00:14:06.098
That's what you got to
do, ask God for something

00:14:06.098 --> 00:14:07.190
and then believe it.

00:14:07.190 --> 00:14:09.192
Now, faith without works is
dead, you got to be willing

00:14:09.192 --> 00:14:13.061
to hustle, because the
hustle's sold separately now.

00:14:13.061 --> 00:14:15.285
The dream is free, you
can dream all day long,

00:14:15.285 --> 00:14:17.480
but the hustle's sold separately.

00:14:17.480 --> 00:14:20.713
God willed all of us to do
the gift that he put in us.

00:14:20.713 --> 00:14:22.829
Now, you gift might be attached to a job,

00:14:22.829 --> 00:14:24.602
some of you all should
been done quit your job

00:14:24.602 --> 00:14:26.749
and tried your business idea.

00:14:26.749 --> 00:14:30.243
But now you, I got these
bills, I can't quit.

00:14:30.243 --> 00:14:33.778
Tell you what, if you don't quit,

00:14:33.778 --> 00:14:36.940
if you do not quit and
go fulfill your dream,

00:14:36.940 --> 00:14:40.079
you ain't ever going to
be happy, it ain't no way.

00:14:40.079 --> 00:14:41.722
Because you ain't living in your dream.

00:14:41.722 --> 00:14:44.760
You've got to do it, just
take the leap of faith.

00:14:44.760 --> 00:14:45.763
What you waiting on?

00:14:45.763 --> 00:14:47.687
God big, God hold you up.

00:14:47.687 --> 00:14:51.177
You going to a couple and tears
on your way once you jump,

00:14:51.177 --> 00:14:52.948
because when you jump,
just know this right away.

00:14:52.948 --> 00:14:55.866
The parachute not going
to open right away.

00:14:55.866 --> 00:14:58.152
When you jump, you going to
hit the edges of the rock

00:14:58.152 --> 00:15:01.207
and all that, but after a while, it opens.

00:15:01.207 --> 00:15:03.418
But it ain't going to
open if you don't jump.

00:15:03.418 --> 00:15:05.635
Now, you can stay safe,
you can stand on the cliff

00:15:05.635 --> 00:15:08.749
watching everybody
soaring by and never jump.

00:15:08.749 --> 00:15:11.352
Keep that parachute on your
back tucked in the pack.

00:15:11.352 --> 00:15:13.988
Be nice and safe, don't
jump, but you going to watch

00:15:13.988 --> 00:15:16.925
a lot of people soaring by
with their parachute on.

00:15:16.925 --> 00:15:20.021
Until you jump, you
will never have the life

00:15:20.021 --> 00:15:21.630
that God wants you to have.

00:15:21.630 --> 00:15:24.945
If you ain't going to
jump, man, you got to jump.

00:15:24.945 --> 00:15:26.853
Just jump, just go.

00:15:26.853 --> 00:15:28.395
- I wanted to ask you, how do you overcome

00:15:28.395 --> 00:15:30.145
the fears and doubts?

00:15:31.082 --> 00:15:33.971
- I mean, look, the fears
and doubts are a part of it.

00:15:33.971 --> 00:15:35.619
Can I be honest with you?

00:15:35.619 --> 00:15:38.951
Everything I've ever
done started with a fear.

00:15:38.951 --> 00:15:42.132
My walking out on stage,
that starts with a fear.

00:15:42.132 --> 00:15:44.089
When Oprah came and got
me for this life class,

00:15:44.089 --> 00:15:46.078
I told her, I said, "This is like

00:15:46.078 --> 00:15:48.260
"a standup appearance for me."

00:15:48.260 --> 00:15:50.805
I'm back there sweating, I
don't want to talk to nobody.

00:15:50.805 --> 00:15:53.381
I have to overcome fear all the time.

00:15:53.381 --> 00:15:55.833
When I wrote my book, I was afraid.

00:15:55.833 --> 00:15:58.523
When they told me, "We wanted
you to be a game show host,"

00:15:58.523 --> 00:16:00.806
I've never done that, I was afraid.

00:16:00.806 --> 00:16:03.005
When they said, "We wantt
you to do a talk show?",

00:16:03.005 --> 00:16:06.713
I was afraid, I have to
overcome fear all the time.

00:16:06.713 --> 00:16:09.203
But the best way for
me to overcome fear is,

00:16:09.203 --> 00:16:12.614
the dream has to be bigger than the fear.

00:16:12.614 --> 00:16:14.729
That's the only way you
turn around and run at it.

00:16:14.729 --> 00:16:18.896
I just want something so
great, I aim for stuff so big,

00:16:19.771 --> 00:16:22.902
that the dream is bigger than the fear.

00:16:22.902 --> 00:16:25.111
Look at it like this, man.

00:16:25.111 --> 00:16:27.611
If you don't ever go for this,

00:16:29.282 --> 00:16:31.323
would it be better for
you to face the fear

00:16:31.323 --> 00:16:32.830
or just deal with the fact

00:16:32.830 --> 00:16:34.839
that you just never gave it a shot?

00:16:34.839 --> 00:16:36.506
- Face it, definitely.

00:16:36.506 --> 00:16:38.437
- See, that's what, the dream.

00:16:38.437 --> 00:16:41.588
I saw you with your tie on,
I know that makeup mirror,

00:16:41.588 --> 00:16:44.657
that's backstage somewhere
in a dressing room.

00:16:44.657 --> 00:16:47.040
Somebody's hiring guys like you.

00:16:47.040 --> 00:16:49.235
It's no such thing as too old, I'm 57.

00:16:49.235 --> 00:16:51.231
If I went back out there,
I'd get hired tomorrow

00:16:51.231 --> 00:16:55.079
as a standup, if you funny,
there's a marketplace for you.

00:16:55.079 --> 00:16:57.368
Now, look--
- Start where you are, right?

00:16:57.368 --> 00:16:58.865
- Just where you at.
- Start where you are.

00:16:58.865 --> 00:17:01.995
- Now, behind me is a sign, and I want you

00:17:01.995 --> 00:17:05.727
to take a look at this
sign as they pull the cord.

00:17:05.727 --> 00:17:06.911
Can you see this?

00:17:06.911 --> 00:17:08.143
- [Steve] Yeah, I'm looking at it.

00:17:08.143 --> 00:17:10.507
- [Man] Here we go.

00:17:10.507 --> 00:17:12.922
- [Woman] Terry, help her!

00:17:12.922 --> 00:17:17.089
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:17:22.774 --> 00:17:25.390
- Alright, Mr. Harvey, I want
to read the last paragraph

00:17:25.390 --> 00:17:27.619
of the proclamation, it says,

00:17:27.619 --> 00:17:31.079
"Now, therefore, I,
Mayor Frank G. Jackson,

00:17:31.079 --> 00:17:33.498
"the 56th Mayor of the City of Cleveland,

00:17:33.498 --> 00:17:37.000
"do hereby offer this
proclamation in recognition

00:17:37.000 --> 00:17:39.245
"of the Steve Harvey Day.

00:17:39.245 --> 00:17:41.741
"I invite all Clevelanders to join me

00:17:41.741 --> 00:17:45.130
"in congratulating Mr.
Harvey on his success

00:17:45.130 --> 00:17:47.637
"and commending him on his contribution

00:17:47.637 --> 00:17:50.168
"to the City of Cleveland
and the community."

00:17:50.168 --> 00:17:53.638
One more time, happy
birthday to Steve Harvey.

00:17:53.638 --> 00:17:56.241
- [Crowd] Happy birthday!

00:17:56.241 --> 00:17:58.241
- Thank you all, wow, man.

00:17:59.257 --> 00:18:04.067
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:18:04.067 --> 00:18:06.091
That's the best.

00:18:06.091 --> 00:18:09.080
- What are your thoughts
about all of this?

00:18:09.080 --> 00:18:11.416
- I mean, my family, man, but you know.

00:18:11.416 --> 00:18:13.749
- I love that, look at that.

00:18:16.297 --> 00:18:20.314
- I learned everything
I know about survival

00:18:20.314 --> 00:18:22.676
on that block right there,

00:18:22.676 --> 00:18:26.180
with them dudes you
looking at right there.

00:18:26.180 --> 00:18:28.628
That's my mama's house.

00:18:28.628 --> 00:18:32.545
(audience cheering applauding)

00:18:45.701 --> 00:18:47.525
- Thank you so much for
watching, I made this video

00:18:47.525 --> 00:18:50.007
because TishNStan asked me to.

00:18:50.007 --> 00:18:52.097
So, if there's a famous
entrepreneur that you want me

00:18:52.097 --> 00:18:54.255
to profile next, leave
it in the comments below

00:18:54.255 --> 00:18:55.477
and I'll see what I can do.

00:18:55.477 --> 00:18:57.970
I'd also like to know which
of Steve's top 10 rules

00:18:57.970 --> 00:18:59.902
impacted you the most and why.

00:18:59.902 --> 00:19:02.036
Leave it in the comments,
I'll join in the discussion.

00:19:02.036 --> 00:19:04.696
Thank you so much for
watching, continue to believe,

00:19:04.696 --> 00:19:06.529
and I'll see you soon.

00:19:12.289 --> 00:19:16.286
- Whatever you think riches
is, that's your definition.

00:19:16.286 --> 00:19:17.634
There's a survey that says

00:19:17.634 --> 00:19:20.222
riches and success is being happy.

00:19:20.222 --> 00:19:22.377
Well, all you have to do then is determine

00:19:22.377 --> 00:19:25.724
what is it that makes you
happy and start down that path.

00:19:25.724 --> 00:19:28.903
Now, to find true success,
I believe that you've got

00:19:28.903 --> 00:19:31.444
to do some work, because it's not free.

00:19:31.444 --> 00:19:34.433
Everybody would love to
wake up and just be happy

00:19:34.433 --> 00:19:36.833
and bubbly, but it requires some work.

00:19:36.833 --> 00:19:39.973
So I want to share with
you something from my book,

00:19:39.973 --> 00:19:43.140
chapter 11, there is no self-made man.

00:19:44.792 --> 00:19:47.828
Now, most of us want to
believe that we're independent,

00:19:47.828 --> 00:19:50.315
that if we set our minds to do something,

00:19:50.315 --> 00:19:52.548
simply it can get done.

00:19:52.548 --> 00:19:56.468
Well, I got news for you,
unless you look to others,

00:19:56.468 --> 00:20:00.079
you can work twice as
hard to get half as much.

00:20:00.079 --> 00:20:02.696
Sometimes you need a partner in the deal

00:20:02.696 --> 00:20:04.541
in order to aid you along the way.

00:20:04.541 --> 00:20:09.013
There is nothing wrong with
asking for what you want.

00:20:09.013 --> 00:20:10.978
You know, for a long time I used to think

00:20:10.978 --> 00:20:14.276
that the path to success
was going at it alone.

00:20:14.276 --> 00:20:16.782
Because I was always busy priding myself

00:20:16.782 --> 00:20:19.512
on not asking for help.

00:20:19.512 --> 00:20:21.708
I was homeless, I didn't
want to ask for help.

00:20:21.708 --> 00:20:24.450
I lived in a car, I didn't
want to ask for help.

00:20:24.450 --> 00:20:26.244
And I almost missed out.

00:20:26.244 --> 00:20:28.330
I didn't realize how
many people were willing

00:20:28.330 --> 00:20:31.771
to have discussions with me about success.

00:20:31.771 --> 00:20:33.446
You know, most people that are successful,

00:20:33.446 --> 00:20:35.950
if you ask them for help,
they'll give it to you.

00:20:35.950 --> 00:20:39.742
I'm talking about advice,
principles, solutions.

00:20:39.742 --> 00:20:44.239
Not money, see one thing
that's never a good idea,

00:20:44.239 --> 00:20:46.840
don't walk up to a wealthy
person and just ask for money.

00:20:46.840 --> 00:20:49.122
You know how many times
they done got that?

00:20:49.122 --> 00:20:52.142
But if you're interested
in learning how to fish,

00:20:52.142 --> 00:20:54.568
a lot of people will
teach you how to fish,

00:20:54.568 --> 00:20:56.665
as opposed to giving you a fish sandwich.

00:20:56.665 --> 00:20:58.168
Because they know if they
give you the fish sandwich,

00:20:58.168 --> 00:21:00.412
you going to eat it, you
going to have to come back.

00:21:00.412 --> 00:21:02.290
A lot of people have
helped me along the way.

00:21:02.290 --> 00:21:05.738
Magic Johnson, Oprah
Winfrey, the President.

00:21:05.738 --> 00:21:08.022
I've had some conversations
with some people

00:21:08.022 --> 00:21:10.248
who have it together and they've taught me

00:21:10.248 --> 00:21:11.946
many things about succeeding.

00:21:11.946 --> 00:21:15.506
You might think that
requesting help is a huge ask,

00:21:15.506 --> 00:21:18.403
but it's not, people don't
mind sharing knowledge.

00:21:18.403 --> 00:21:21.143
What is knowledge unless it's shared?

00:21:21.143 --> 00:21:23.272
If you have knowledge
but you never share it,

00:21:23.272 --> 00:21:25.042
how we know you got it?

00:21:25.042 --> 00:21:26.559
(audience laughing)

00:21:26.559 --> 00:21:30.837
And just remember, there is
no shame in wanting something.

00:21:30.837 --> 00:21:33.182
This whole world is based
on wanting something.

00:21:33.182 --> 00:21:35.395
You know, don't sit up
and listen to some group,

00:21:35.395 --> 00:21:38.039
wanting something is a sin, no, it's not.

00:21:38.039 --> 00:21:39.754
You got to want something,
the scripture says

00:21:39.754 --> 00:21:42.658
a man without a dream or
a vision shall perish.

00:21:42.658 --> 00:21:44.425
So the day you quit wanting something,

00:21:44.425 --> 00:21:46.726
you might as well push your
chips up to the window,

00:21:46.726 --> 00:21:49.701
it's a wrap, so lose the shame

00:21:49.701 --> 00:21:53.430
and you'll have access to more power.

00:21:53.430 --> 00:21:56.034
Here's the key that I
wanted to tell you about.

00:21:56.034 --> 00:21:59.527
Success is all about
building relationships.

00:21:59.527 --> 00:22:02.279
It's not what you know, it's who you know.

00:22:02.279 --> 00:22:05.911
Some people might not step up
when you ask them for help,

00:22:05.911 --> 00:22:07.769
they might not, but guess what?

00:22:07.769 --> 00:22:10.522
The worst thing can happen to you,

00:22:10.522 --> 00:22:15.210
if somebody refuses you,
you didn't have it anyway.

00:22:15.210 --> 00:22:16.871
What are you worrying about that for?

00:22:16.871 --> 00:22:19.390
Well, they might say no or
they might turn me down.

00:22:19.390 --> 00:22:21.777
Ask people, you never know.

00:22:21.777 --> 00:22:26.473
Suppose they say yes, that
could be the turning factor.

00:22:26.473 --> 00:22:28.870
But there are some
principles that will increase

00:22:28.870 --> 00:22:31.164
your chances of getting success.

00:22:31.164 --> 00:22:34.652
Know your worth, don't let
nobody else determine it.

00:22:34.652 --> 00:22:38.409
And don't assume anything,
people aren't mind readers.

00:22:38.409 --> 00:22:41.107
They don't know what you
thinking, don't assume they know,

00:22:41.107 --> 00:22:43.498
unless you ask with specifics.

00:22:43.498 --> 00:22:47.331
And then recognize that
no is not a rejection.

00:22:48.429 --> 00:22:50.399
Every time you hear no, it moves you

00:22:50.399 --> 00:22:52.999
one step closer to a yes.

00:22:52.999 --> 00:22:54.916
Everybody can't say no.

00:22:55.854 --> 00:22:58.196
Not unless you got a harebrained idea.

00:22:58.196 --> 00:22:59.698
(audience laughing)

00:22:59.698 --> 00:23:03.386
And just remember that success
is about building a world

00:23:03.386 --> 00:23:06.754
that looks the way you
want it to, nobody else.

00:23:06.754 --> 00:23:09.632
Never be afraid to reinvent yourself.

00:23:09.632 --> 00:23:14.550
My career, my entire career
is a study in reinvention.

00:23:14.550 --> 00:23:17.304
I started out as a comedian, that was it.

00:23:17.304 --> 00:23:21.102
I never planned on hosting a radio show,

00:23:21.102 --> 00:23:24.963
hosting a game show, or
hosting a daytime talk show.

00:23:24.963 --> 00:23:27.912
I never did, writing books, none of it.

00:23:27.912 --> 00:23:30.212
Making movies, none of it.

00:23:30.212 --> 00:23:34.420
Reinvention happens when
you diversify your gift.

00:23:34.420 --> 00:23:37.222
There lies your greatest
secret for success.

00:23:37.222 --> 00:23:40.710
You've to discover your gift,
and when you discover it,

00:23:40.710 --> 00:23:43.653
you got to soak it, you
got to wring it out, man.

00:23:43.653 --> 00:23:45.443
You got to diversify it.

00:23:45.443 --> 00:23:48.462
Most of us only have one talent.

00:23:48.462 --> 00:23:50.829
But do you know that that's all you need?

00:23:50.829 --> 00:23:54.083
Mine happens to be to take information

00:23:54.083 --> 00:23:57.844
and immediately transfer it
into other kinds of platforms.

00:23:57.844 --> 00:24:01.165
Now, when I was younger,
I actually thought

00:24:01.165 --> 00:24:03.080
that I could only do that with comedy.

00:24:03.080 --> 00:24:06.033
But as I've gotten older
I discovered through

00:24:06.033 --> 00:24:08.744
diversification that it was
a little bit more than that,

00:24:08.744 --> 00:24:10.804
that I could also take information,

00:24:10.804 --> 00:24:13.783
immediately transfer it into inspiration.

00:24:13.783 --> 00:24:15.852
I could turn it into motivation.

00:24:15.852 --> 00:24:17.853
I can offer it as guidance.

00:24:17.853 --> 00:24:19.510
So now, sitting on a talk show,

00:24:19.510 --> 00:24:21.773
I actually have something to talk about.

00:24:21.773 --> 00:24:24.624
All the failed marriages, I
got something to talk about.

00:24:24.624 --> 00:24:26.984
The being homeless, I got
something to talk about.

00:24:26.984 --> 00:24:29.763
Being dead broke, I got
something to talk about.

00:24:29.763 --> 00:24:32.130
Having bad credit, tax problems,

00:24:32.130 --> 00:24:33.335
I got something to talk about.

00:24:33.335 --> 00:24:34.608
Whatever hole you've been
in, I done just about

00:24:34.608 --> 00:24:38.412
drug myself through it,
but I came out of all of it

00:24:38.412 --> 00:24:42.898
because I was not afraid
to diversify my gift.

00:24:42.898 --> 00:24:45.283
Even the book, Act Like
A Lady, Think Like A Man,

00:24:45.283 --> 00:24:47.800
it was all about me diversifying the gift.

00:24:47.800 --> 00:24:50.934
Okay, I had taken two failed marriages

00:24:50.934 --> 00:24:54.683
and I had taken the love for my daughters

00:24:54.683 --> 00:24:56.549
and I combined those things.

00:24:56.549 --> 00:25:00.729
I taught my daughters
what I knew about men.

00:25:00.729 --> 00:25:02.945
Now, little did I discover
that I had a little

00:25:02.945 --> 00:25:06.254
over four million
daughters in this country.

00:25:06.254 --> 00:25:08.130
Cousins, and nieces, and stuff like that

00:25:08.130 --> 00:25:09.971
who needed that same information.

00:25:09.971 --> 00:25:13.279
And that was a huge part for
me, to take that information

00:25:13.279 --> 00:25:15.108
and turn it into a book that turned it

00:25:15.108 --> 00:25:19.975
into a megastar movie and
produced a lot of things for me,

00:25:19.975 --> 00:25:21.787
but it also helped a lot of people.

00:25:21.787 --> 00:25:24.840
One of the other tricks
for reinventing yourself is

00:25:24.840 --> 00:25:28.896
not letting your background
become a limitation.

00:25:28.896 --> 00:25:32.238
If you take that
background that you're from

00:25:32.238 --> 00:25:37.071
and never let it define you,
but allow it to redefine you,

00:25:37.071 --> 00:25:38.669
all that stuff works for the good.

00:25:38.669 --> 00:25:40.898
Do you understand that
you needed everything

00:25:40.898 --> 00:25:42.853
that's happened to you to happen to you

00:25:42.853 --> 00:25:44.610
in the exact order that it's happened

00:25:44.610 --> 00:25:47.112
in order for you to be the
person that you are today?

00:25:47.112 --> 00:25:50.193
All that failing and getting
over, you needed all of that.

00:25:50.193 --> 00:25:53.124
(audience applauding)

00:25:53.124 --> 00:25:56.622
It's good to be steeped in
the traditions of your gift,

00:25:56.622 --> 00:25:58.958
but don't get stuck in them.

00:25:58.958 --> 00:26:01.098
Look, if your gift is baking, don't assume

00:26:01.098 --> 00:26:04.015
that there's only one way to do it.

00:26:04.015 --> 00:26:06.413
If you bake, bake, but you can't just bake

00:26:06.413 --> 00:26:08.754
for people you know, bake
for people you don't know.

00:26:08.754 --> 00:26:11.184
You're a musician, let yourself explore

00:26:11.184 --> 00:26:12.764
other types of music.

00:26:12.764 --> 00:26:14.518
I'll tell you an example, The Roots,

00:26:14.518 --> 00:26:16.369
who play on Jimmy Fallon's show,

00:26:16.369 --> 00:26:20.879
they steeped in hip hop, but
they're also great musicians.

00:26:20.879 --> 00:26:24.036
So what they do is, they
take all of that talent

00:26:24.036 --> 00:26:27.147
and now guess what, hip hop, jazz,

00:26:27.147 --> 00:26:31.377
R&amp;B, classic, pop, rock, they didn't just

00:26:31.377 --> 00:26:33.621
get stuck on hip hop, I'm
doing hip hop, that's it.

00:26:33.621 --> 00:26:34.915
No, they do whatever.

00:26:34.915 --> 00:26:38.553
LL Cool J, hip hop, one of
the top actors on TV today.

00:26:38.553 --> 00:26:42.394
Queen Latifah, hip hop, big
actor right now, you get it?

00:26:42.394 --> 00:26:44.650
Jerry Seinfeld, nothing but a comedian.

00:26:44.650 --> 00:26:46.552
One of the biggest actors on TV today.

00:26:46.552 --> 00:26:49.660
Remember, you can win if you're not afraid

00:26:49.660 --> 00:26:52.155
to reinvent yourself, stop getting stuck.

00:26:52.155 --> 00:26:54.443
Just go ahead and give
it a try, you never know.

00:26:54.443 --> 00:26:57.113
You also need some outside perspective.

00:26:57.113 --> 00:26:59.592
If you listen to people
that's close to you,

00:26:59.592 --> 00:27:02.082
that have your best interests outside,

00:27:02.082 --> 00:27:04.879
you can use these outside observers

00:27:04.879 --> 00:27:08.188
to gain knowledge to assess yourself.

00:27:08.188 --> 00:27:11.149
And when you reach out to
get these outside opinions,

00:27:11.149 --> 00:27:13.258
be open, keep your emotions in check.

00:27:13.258 --> 00:27:16.342
You can't say that about, just
keep your emotions in check.

00:27:16.342 --> 00:27:18.252
Now, from there you
going to have a good feel

00:27:18.252 --> 00:27:20.567
about what your strengths
and weaknesses are,

00:27:20.567 --> 00:27:22.413
and you can work on them to build them.

